      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: distribution — shareable deep links, export/import, dashboard-design skill",
        "body": "> Make a dashboard shareable and portable: link straight to a tab, export/import a workspace as JSON, and give agents a workflow to review the layouts they build.\n\nCloses #101155, #101156. Addresses #101154 (see the deep-link note below). **Stacked on #101098** — targets `main` with a cumulative diff.\n\n## What's in this PR\n- **Shareable deep links (#101154)** — the active tab is encoded in the URL as `?ws=<slug>`, so a link resolves straight to a tab and browser back/forward walks tab history (via `pushState`/`popstate`); an unknown slug falls back gracefully to the first tab. This PR **locks that contract with regression tests** (slug↔query round-trip preserving `plugin`/`id`; back-compat resolve; unknown-slug fallback) and documents in-code why the tab key stays a query param rather than a `/plugin/dashboard/:slug` path segment. **See \"Deep-link scope\" below — this is a deliberate, documented deviation for your review.**\n- **Export / import (#101155)** — export the workspace (or a tab subset) to a timestamped JSON download; import parses the file, coerces every custom widget to `pending`, and applies it via the existing `dashboard.workspace.replace` RPC. Any imported custom widget lands in the L5 approval gate — **never auto-approved**.\n- **Dashboard-design skill (#101156)** — `extensions/dashboard/docs/DASHBOARD-DESIGN.md`: an agent-facing snapshot→evaluate→refine→render-check workflow (balance / grouping / binding-coverage / sizing heuristics; smallest-tool refinement; screenshot pairs with the preview widget's browser mode). Convention + doc only; the L5 gate is untouched.\n\n## Deep-link scope (the one deviation — your call)\nIssue #101154 sketched promoting `?ws=` to a `/plugin/dashboard/:slug` **path** route. On investigation that's infeasible inside a plugin PR: `@openclaw/uirouter@0.1.0` is a pinned external package (no in-repo source) that matches routes by **exact `byPath` map lookup** — it has no dynamic-segment support — and `/plugin` is a single route multiplexed by `?plugin=&id=`; an unmatched trailing segment is redirected to `/chat` by the startup guard. The existing `?ws=<slug>` query **already satisfies every behavioral requirement** of a deep link (resolves on load, shareable, bookmarkable, back/forward-navigable, graceful unknown-slug fallback). So this PR keeps the query mechanism, hardens it with regression tests, and documents the constraint in-code. A true path segment needs a core-router or external-package change — an architecture call I've left to you rather than fork the router speculatively.\n\n## Security (import → approval gate)\nImport is **fail-safe by construction**: `sanitizeImportedWorkspace` rewrites every widget-registry entry through `toPendingEntry`, which forces `status: \"pending\"` and **drops any `approvedBy`/`approvedAt`** — so an imported doc claiming `{ status: \"approved\", approvedBy: \"user\" }` is applied as `{ status: \"pending\" }` and its widget can't mount until an operator approves it (mirrors the agent-tool guard `sanitizeAgentWorkspaceReplace`, but forces pending unconditionally because an imported workspace is foreign, untrusted authoring). A custom widget referenced by a tab but missing from the registry is **seeded** a pending entry, so there's no gap where an un-gated custom could mount. Structural validity is enforced **server-side**: `dashboard.workspace.replace` runs `validateWorkspaceDoc`, so a malformed or hostile import is rejected on the wire (surfaced as an error toast), not trusted from the client. Defense in depth: client coerces to pending, server re-validates structure.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** Dashboards weren't shareable (no deep link contract), portable (no export/import), or self-reviewable by the agents that build them. This adds a tested query-based deep-link contract, validated + approval-gated export/import, and an agent design-review skill.\n**Evidence (full local gate, rebased onto the base's 3 seam fixes + integration test, run and read before opening):**\n- `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/dashboard` → **81 passed** (includes the UI↔gateway integration test).\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/lib/dashboard src/pages/plugin` (in `ui/`) → **130 passed** — export/import round-trip, the wire assertion that an imported `approved` widget is sent as `pending`, malformed-JSON + invalid-doc rejection, deep-link round-trip / back-compat / unknown-slug fallback.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check` clean (4 new keys synced across all locales) · `pnpm ui:build` ok · full type-aware `pnpm lint` **exit 0**.\n\n## Dependency note\nNo new dependencies. The only lockfile delta across this stack is the new plugin's own importer entry; `dependency-guard` is red purely because fork PRs can't authorize the dependency-graph head SHA — a one-touch maintainer approval clears it (same as the rest of this stack).\n",
